questions.explanation:
$$
\lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{(2x^2 - 3x + 5)(3x - 1)^{\frac{x}{2}}}{(3x^2 + 5x + 4)\sqrt{(3x + 2)^x}}
$$

$$
= \lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{x^2(2 - \frac{3}{x} + \frac{5}{x^2}) (3x)^{\frac{x}{2}}(1 - \frac{1}{3x})^{\frac{x}{2}}}{x^2(3 + \frac{5}{x} + \frac{4}{x^2}) (3x)^{\frac{x}{2}}(1 + \frac{2}{3x})^{\frac{x}{2}}}
$$

$$
= \lim_{x \to \infty} \frac{(2 - \frac{3}{x} + \frac{5}{x^2}) (1 - \frac{1}{3x})^{\frac{x}{2}}}{(3 + \frac{5}{x} + \frac{4}{x^2}) (1 + \frac{2}{3x})^{\frac{x}{2}}}
$$

As \(x \to \infty\), \( (2 - \frac{3}{x} + \frac{5}{x^2}) \to 2 \) and \( (3 + \frac{5}{x} + \frac{4}{x^2}) \to 3 \).

Also, using the standard limit \( \lim_{t \to \infty} (1 + \frac{a}{t})^{bt} = e^{ab} \):

$$
\lim_{x \to \infty} \left(1 - \frac{1}{3x}\right)^{\frac{x}{2}} = e^{(-1/3)(1/2)} = e^{-1/6}
$$

$$
\lim_{x \to \infty} \left(1 + \frac{2}{3x}\right)^{\frac{x}{2}} = e^{(2/3)(1/2)} = e^{1/3}
$$

Substituting these values back into the limit expression:

$$
= \frac{2}{3} \cdot \frac{e^{-1/6}}{e^{1/3}}
$$

$$
= \frac{2}{3} \cdot e^{-1/6 - 1/3}
$$

$$
= \frac{2}{3} \cdot e^{-1/6 - 2/6}
$$

$$
= \frac{2}{3} \cdot e^{-3/6}
$$

$$
= \frac{2}{3} \cdot e^{-1/2}
$$

$$
= \frac{2}{3\sqrt{e}}
$$
